==== Warming up
#ix("Warm-up", main: true)

No study shows that warming up prevents bouldering injuries. In the knee-injury study, four in five of the injured climbers already had a warm-up routine #src("G9"). In a small study, foam rolling and static stretching#ix("Stretching") didn't change climbing performance#ix("Studies!warm-up and stretching") #src("G39"). Warm-up advice comes from coaches and federations: the German Alpine Club makes a thorough warm-up its first bouldering rule #src("G11"). The routine below is this book's suggestion, built from that advice.

#ctable(
